<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Isabella of Villehardouin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1260–<a href="/years/1312">1312</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Isabella of Villehardouin was Princess of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaea">Achaea</a> from 1289 to 1307, heiress of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-ii-of-villehardouin">William II of Villehardouin</a>. Married first to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-v-of-spain">Philip of Anjou</a>, son of Charles I of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naples">Naples</a>, she was invested with the principality on her marriage to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florent-of-hainaut">Florent of Hainaut</a>, and in 1301 married Philip of Savoy, lord of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piedmont">Piedmont</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-ii-of-naples">Charles II of Naples</a> deprived her of the principality in 1307.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/isabella-of-villehardouin.jpg" alt="Isabella of Villehardouin" width="300" height="417" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Schlumberger, Gustave Léon, 1844-1929 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Isabella_of_Villehardouin.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
